:: history [donotshowinventory] {"position":"1420.0000000000002,19.166666666666657","size":"100,100"}
"The history of this library isn't as long as others," the Librarian states, "but it is far from boring."

"Enigma Reiter designed this library in 2010, but it wasn't fully constructed until 2013. It was inspired by her love of reading  and how libraries bring a special feeling of stepping out of reality."

"There were many things that came to mind when thinking of libraries, that she wanted to share with others."

"She believed they held a magical quality.
She believed they could take readers back in time.
She believed they could allow people to be whoever they want, or hold the most diverse emotions.
She believed they give off a certain intrique, as no one gets what they fully expect.
And Ms. Enigma Reiter believed people left feeling almost alien in the world they came from."

"And since then," the Librarian finishes, "the library has done just that."

I ask who [[Enigma Reiter]] is.

"Did you have another [[question|Librarian]]?"


