:: sections {"position":"1538.9999999999998,239.16666666666669","size":"100,100"}
"There are six sections to the library," the [[Librarian]] says, "Ms. Reiter prided herself on fictional genres, so there are no non-fiction books within these walls."

"And so," she says, "those six sections are as such. There is Fantasy, Historical Fiction, Western, Romance, Mystery, and Science Fiction."

I ask about [[Fantasy]].
I ask about [[Historical Fiction]].
I ask about [[Western]].
I ask about [[Romance]].
I ask about [[Mystery]].
I ask about [[Science Fiction]].
I ask what section is her [[favorite]].


:: sinks {"position":"1095,137.50000000000003","size":"100,100"}
I notice right away that all the sinks are lined with loose sand.

After checking the faucets, not all of them work. Those that do work has something else come out instead of water.

One has flower petals. They settle on the sand, then seem to melt into the sand and disappear.
The other has honey. It slips slowly through the sand, taking some with it, leaving tracks on the way to the drain at the bottom.

[["I guess they don't want their patrons to be clean?"|Restroom]]


